    <!-- 1.8.15 = EdrWatcher's local outbox (queued reports the bastion hasn't ACKed yet) had no
         cap at all. Found live 2026-07-22: a report_token mismatch between bastion state and this
         box's endpoint-config.json (likely a VM snapshot revert after a later re-provision) sent
         every report POST into a permanent 403 loop for 2+ days, silently growing the outbox to
         several hundred files with nobody ever seeing an alert. QueueToOutbox now prunes oldest-
         first (by the existing yyyyMMddHHmmssfff filename prefix, already chronological) before
         every enqueue: hard cap 2000 files, 14-day max age. Does not fix a stuck token itself —
         that still needs a fresh Enable EDR click to re-provision matching tokens on both sides. -->
    <!-- 1.8.16 = SetupRunner's OpenSSH-Win64 re-extraction check only verified sshd.exe existed
         before deciding to skip re-extracting the embedded zip. Found live 2026-07-22 on the test Windows host:
         sftp-server.exe was missing from that folder (most likely Defender real-time protection
         acting on it before an exclusion was ever applied) while sshd.exe survived, so the reverse
         tunnel and plain ssh EncodedCommand execution stayed healthy, but EVERY feature that
         deploys a script via scp (Defender Exclusion, Telemetry block, forensics collection, File
         Backup, etc) silently failed with "scp: Connection closed", and re-running the setup flag
         did nothing because this check never noticed anything was wrong. Now requires
